From 8a5ff11e9127c308a701ee88b8d1ed5d5a991687 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:08:39 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] 3D options, the sentences for the person, and ten
 languages

Enable 3D, Render Resolution per Eye (50, 75 and 100 %: the window of the view has the render resolution and Stereo KWin shows it at the size of the area, so the program stretches nothing) and Display Settings in the View strip; a message above
the view says when the two views cannot be given (no stereo surface, limits not told,
limits zero); the 3D View action no longer fails without a sentence. The program's sentences
are translated into the ten languages of the edition and embedded.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
